 "purpose": "The Maten (unit conversion) screen: an Oefenaar subclass that adds choosing units yourself, level choice and a result that also counts table mistakes.",
 "details": "MatenOefenaar reuses everything of Oefenaar (series, free practice, result, repeat bin) and only adds what Maten does differently: oefen() picks the unit set ('zelf' lets the child tick units, 'alles' mixes everything for the school year, otherwise one category from kern/wiskunde/eenheden), asks the level, remembers the exercise for 'Verder waar je was' (app.onthoud_oefening) and plays the form 'vrij', 'reeks' or 'tabel'; hervat() replays the stored choice. The questions are made lazily one at a time (een_voor_een) by E.Maten. A result row counts as a mistake when the answer was wrong or the unit table was wrong (is_fout), and the mistake lines explain both. herhalen() and spiekbrief() are module-level entry points used by the curriculum registry.",
 "module_docstring": "Eenheden omzetten (Maten): de Oefenaar met de eenhedentabel (terminal/tabel.py).",
